@tradition postcard-night
// Postcard night (0.60.7): write a card home (the writing hobby's tradition) at the booth row; it goes out with the
// next mail run. Eklund keeps the cards and the box (the deck architect's postcard box).
k: 446
title: Postcard night
when: weekly thursday
at: 18:45-19:45
min: 20
where: 3 room Call-home booths: bench
where: 3 room Promenade: bench
hold: 1
who: eklund-leila always, calls-home 45%, quiet-corner 25%, everyone 10%
anim: read
host: eklund-leila
from: eklund-leila
invite: host=eklund-leila odds=30% line="Postcard night, by the booths. I've got spare cards. Write one home?"


== mail
- Postcard night tomorrow at {time} by the booths. Cards on the table, pens in the pot. The mail run takes them Friday.

== ask
- Postcard night. Write one home. They'll love it.
- Cards are out by the booths. Five minutes, a card home.

== here
- What do I say? I always say the food's good.   #funny
- Short is fine. They just want to hear from you.   #warm
- Anyone got a pen that works?

== thanks
- At booth row you write a card home, pin it in the mail box, and it goes out with the next mail run.   #warm

== chatter
- Postcard night later. My gran keeps every one.   #warm
- I write the same card every week. Nobody minds.   #funny
- Mail run goes Friday. Get your card in tonight.
